The '''Comarca de Sant Cristòfor''' ({{lang|ca|Comarca de Sant Cristòfor}}) is the most populous and economically significant of the thirteen [[comarca]]s of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. It contains the city of [[Sant Cristòfor]], the national capital and the largest city in the country, as well as two major islands in the [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]] that form a separate municipality. The comarca had a population of 5,178,000 in 2026, making it the most populous second-level administrative division in Balboa.

The comarca is divided into two [[municipalitat]]s (municipalities): the '''Municipalitat de Sant Cristòfor''' (the mainland city) and the '''Municipalitat de les Illes''' (the islands of [[Illa del Portal]] and [[Illa Daurada]]).

== Geography ==

[[File:Badia de Sant Cristofor aerial.png|thumb|right|300px|Aerial view of the Badia de Sant Cristòfor, with Illa Daurada (left) and Illa del Portal (right) at the bay mouth.]]

The comarca occupies the central portion of the Shendan coast of Estret Province. It is bounded by the [[Riu Besòs]] to the south (bordering [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]]), the [[Riu Llobregat]] to the north (bordering [[Els Aiguamolls]] and [[Les Planes (comarca)|Les Planes]]), and the [[Serralada d'Estret]] to the east (bordering [[Baix Llevant]]). The western boundary is the [[Shendan Ocean]] coast, dominated by the [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]], a large sheltered bay that has defined the city's history and economy since its founding.

The [[Península de la Barceloneta]] extends from the mainland into the bay, forming the northern arm of the bay mouth and creating a natural breakwater. The southern shore of the bay is the city's original harbour and waterfront district.

The comarca has a total area of 2,625 km², of which approximately 2,534 km² is land and 91 km² is water (the islands and coastal waters within the comarca boundary).

=== Islands ===

{{main|Illa del Portal|Illa Daurada}}

The Badia de Sant Cristòfor contains three islands, two of which are substantial and permanently inhabited:

